Makes three changes on block functionality:
1. Block caching setup is moved to set in the main `acf_blocks` array in `THEME_SETTINGS` rather than in a separate one. This is just to be more consistent, because there's no actual reason to have separate arrays for preventing block cache per block, since we are already listing all blocks in one array.
```
  'acf_blocks' => [
    [
      'name'          => 'form',
      'title'         => 'Form block',
      'prevent_cache' => true // Default value false
    ],
    [
      'name'          => 'random',
      'title'         => 'A random block',
    ]
  ],
```
2. Added a hook `air_acf_block_maybe_enable_cache` to modify block-level caching from elsewhere.
3. Added a hook `air_acf_blocks_example_data` so we can build example data outside of `functions.php` to keep it from bloating. The example data can still be set in `acf_blocks` array and when it's done, the hook will have no effect on blocks example data. 
```
add_filter( 'air_acf_example_data', __NAMESPACE__ . '\air_acf_blocks_example_data', 10, 1 );
/**
 * Build example data for ACF Block previews
 * 
 * @param array $data Example data
 * @return array Modified example data
 */
function acf_set_example_data( $data ) {
  $text = 'Lorem ipsum dolor';
  $wysiwyg = '<p>Nam molestie nec tortor. <a href="#">Donec placerat</a> leo sit amet velit. Vestibulum id justo ut vitae massa. <strong>Proin in dolor mauris consequat aliquam.</strong> Donec ipsum, vestibulum ullamcorper venenatis augue. Aliquam tempus nisi in auctor vulputate, erat felis pellentesque augue nec, pellentesque lectus justo nec erat. Aliquam et nisl. Quisque sit amet dolor in justo pretium condimentum.</p>';
  $wide_img = 2;
  $person_img = 23;
  
  return [
    'title-content' => [
      'bg' => $wide_img,
      'title' => $text,
      'content' => $wysiwyg,
    ],
    'contacts' => [
      'area_title' => $text,
      'persons' =>  [
        'name' => 'John Smith',
        'image' => $person_img,
      ],
      [
        'name' => 'Pocahontas',
        'image' => $person_img,
      ],
    ]
  ]
}

